# three-speeds-one-corridor — plan 23 K2b.
#
# A scout, a robot and a miner walking the SAME corridor in the same
# tick loop, and pulling apart at the ratio of their rates.
#
# ── Why one corridor and not three runs ─────────────────────────
#
# K0's twin scenarios measure a class against a wall, and they have to
# be two files because the same hex cannot be both rubble and wall.  A
# speed measurement has no such problem, and putting all three in one
# world is strictly stronger: same tick, same field rebuild, same
# occupancy pass, one clock.  A per-ROSTER speed — the defect `wave_
# damage` actually shipped with in plan 12 B2, one axis over — keeps
# these three in formation, and no single-class scenario can see it.
#
# ── The arithmetic, so a reader can check it without running it ──
#
# A tick is 1/1.5 s.  An enemy banks `speed x tick_seconds` and steps
# whenever a whole hex is due (plan 23 K2a), so after nine ticks:
#
#   scout 2.5 hex/s -> 1.667 hex/tick -> 15 hexes
#   robot 1.5 hex/s -> 1.0   hex/tick ->  9 hexes
#   miner 1.0 hex/s -> 0.667 hex/tick ->  6 hexes
#
# ⚠⚠ **This file is the repo's witness for `@M017`, and it does not
# take nine ticks to become one — it takes THREE.**  2.5 x (1.0/1.5) is
# 1.6666666666666665, and three of them sum to 4.999999999999999, a
# hair under five.  `ENEMY_PROGRESS_EPSILON` is what releases that
# fifth hex; zero it and this file goes red at `enemy 0 15 0` below
# (measured: it reads 16) while the robot's and the miner's lines on
# the same tick stay green.  That is the guard `@M014` measured as
# UNREACHABLE, made reachable by shipping a class whose speed is not
# 1.5 — and `scripts/validate.sh` fails on it, so the second gate sees
# it too.
#
# ── The world ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   one corridor of grass, thirty-one hexes:  (30, 0) -> (0, 0)
#   core at (0, 0) — no wall, no tower, nothing to stop anybody
#   scout at (20, 0), robot at (25, 0), miner at (30, 0)
#
# ⚠ The three start APART and in that order — fastest in front — so
# nobody ever queues behind anybody and every reading is the class's
# own pace rather than a traffic jam.  `23_k2b_the_scout.loft`
# § A longer stride is still checked hex by hex is where the queue is
# measured on purpose.

echo three speeds down one corridor: 2.5, 1.5 and 1.0 hex/s

do toggle_mode

# The core is where the target is — `play_core` reads the marker, so
# without this there is nothing for the field to point at.
do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target
count markers 1 1

do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag 30 0 0 0
count painted 31 31

# ── The roster, authored rather than spawned ────────────────────
#
# `place` (plan 18 S1a) puts an enemy down healthy and WALKING — no
# spawn marker, no wave, and no pre-walk window to subtract from every
# reading below.  Heading 3 is WEST, which is `(q - 1, r)` on both row
# parities, so a heading can never change `r`.
place 20 0 scout 3
place 25 0 robot 3
place 30 0 miner 3

count alive 3 3
enemy 0 20 0
enemy 1 25 0
enemy 2 30 0
enemies distinct
enemies passable

# ── One tick, and the three are already three ───────────────────
#
# ⚠ **The miner has not moved at all**, and that is the reading that
# says a speed is a RATE rather than a tick count.  It banked two
# thirds of a hex and owes nothing, so it stands still — where the old
# mover advanced every enemy exactly one hex because a tick WAS a hex
# (`@X058`).  The scout banked 1.667 and released one, carrying the
# other two thirds into the next tick rather than losing it.
tick 1
enemy 0 19 0
enemy 1 24 0
enemy 2 30 0

# ── Three ticks: the spread is visible ──────────────────────────
#
# The scout has released 5 hexes, the robot 3 and the miner 2 — and
# the miner's two arrived on ticks 2 and 3, never on tick 1.
tick 2
enemy 0 15 0
enemy 1 22 0
enemy 2 28 0
enemies distinct

# ── Nine ticks: 15 / 9 / 6, exactly the rates ───────────────────
tick 6
enemy 0 5 0
enemy 1 16 0
enemy 2 24 0
enemies distinct
enemies passable
count alive 3 3

# ⚠ Nothing has been attacked and nothing has arrived: the corridor is
# open all the way to the core, so this file measures WALKING and only
# walking.  A drained wallet here would mean somebody got home early.
count targets 0 0
wallet 200 200

snap k2b-three-speeds-one-corridor

# ── And the order never inverts ─────────────────────────────────
#
# Six more ticks: the scout is home and nibbling, the robot is still
# walking and the miner is not halfway.  ⚠ This is the reading that
# would survive a re-baseline of the numbers above — whatever the
# timestep, the fast class arrives first.
tick 6
enemy 0 0 0
enemy 1 10 0
enemy 2 20 0
count targets 0 0
